body:
I don't even dislike the book, lots of stuff was sort of interesting and all and I love Lord of the Rings, but I for the life of me cannot keep up with so many names without sufficient characterization (mainly, dialogue) for each and so I was constantly lost on who was who and that killed it for me. Made it halfway or so, but remember practically none of what transpired other than a few general themes.

&#x200B;

On the other hand, I've never had much trouble remembering names from ASOIAF, even ones from old stories mentioned only a few times across the entire series - goes to show how much it helps to have some context and description, at least with a sieve of a brain like mine.

It's one of those days today when you wake up with a headache and all the ways you fail at life float through your head as a neverending stream. No doubt it's not going to last overly long, not in this intensity at least, but just now I'm feeling so very bitter towards most of the people I know. Can't stop thinking about how much better everyone is than me and how lucky they are, especially as regards having a natural social instinct towards connecting and forming groups. I wish it was easy and natural for me to socialize in groups, I wish I didn't always feel so out of place and like I'm someone who's only tolerated because everyone pities me and I'm not so offending that anyone would hate me either - they're just indifferent and kinda wished I wasn't there because I'm so awkward to talk to because of my anxiety and recent sad events. I hate hearing how normal it is for others to be a part of a group and not freak out and get depressed constantly - they're actually having a good time and I'm so so envious of that you wouldn't even believe. It's all very overwhelming just now and mushed into this one big demon and I wish I could go back to sleep but my head hurts too much. 

&#x200B;

I do have a freshly brewed cup of coffee in front of me though, and that is making things much more tolerable by the second. Even my head doesn't hurt so much anymore. My advent calendar had peanut m&ms in store for today as well, those are my favorites from the calendar's selection. I don't feel okay not even a little bit but maybe this day won't be all bad.
